// Temporary port aid, not pack content - delete when the GregTech port is done.
//
// KubeJS aborts the WHOLE ServerEvents.recipes callback the first time an ingredient fails to
// resolve, so one renamed id hides every id after it and every recipe below it is silently never
// registered. That is why the Micro Universe Orb once showed a single recipe: the script died on
// gtceu:endstone_plutonium_ore at line 114 and only the recipe above it survived.
//
// This resolves every literal id and tag in the ported scripts up front, so one /reload reports
// every problem at once instead of one launch per problem. It reads registries directly rather than
// building ingredients: Ingredient.of on a missing id throws, which is the failure being diagnosed.
//
// Covers every ported script: greenhouse, gtceu, micro_universe_orb, ore_processing_plant,
// coil_multiblock, mega_fusion, allthemodium, starforge, miner, neural_node,
// superheated_pyrolyzing_oven and apiary. Not covered: ids the greenhouse script builds from
// Botany Pots data, and the ids apiary_recipes.js reads out of Productive Bees' own data files -
// that script checks each of those against the registry itself and reports what it left out.
//
// From apiary_recipes.js these are deliberately absent, because they are not items: the recipe
// TYPES productivebees:advanced_beehive and productivebees:centrifuge, the ingredient type
// productivebees:component, the data key productivebees:bee_type, the ENTITY types
// productivebees:{configurable,creeper,lumber,quarry}_bee and minecraft:bee, the legacy tag names
// forge:pollen / forge:wax and the tag names c:pollens / c:wax (all four only ever compared
// against, never used), and c:crude_oil, which is a FLUID tag and would read as an empty item tag.
//
// Ids the scripts BUILD by concatenation are listed by hand, because a text scan cannot see them:
// miner.js composes gtceu:<tier>_machine_hull, gtceu:<tier>_sensor and #gtceu:circuits/<tier> for
// nine tiers. That blind spot is exactly what let gtceu:uhv_world_data_scanner fail while this
// check reported every id resolving. gtceu:uhv_sensor is deliberately absent from that list: it
// does not exist, and miner.js now substitutes a UV sensor for the UHV scanner. The 20 items from
// mods ATM10 does not ship (Croptopia, Thermal, Naturalist, four Delight addons) are absent too:
// neural_node_recipes.js skips those recipes itself and reports the count, so listing them here
// would report a problem that is already handled.
//
// Named to sort first so it runs before the scripts that can abort.

const $BuiltInRegistries = Java.loadClass('net.minecraft.core.registries.BuiltInRegistries')
const $ResourceLocation = Java.loadClass('net.minecraft.resources.ResourceLocation')
const $TagKey = Java.loadClass('net.minecraft.tags.TagKey')
const $Registries = Java.loadClass('net.minecraft.core.registries.Registries')

// Ids that must not exist. If a check ever reports everything as fine, these are what catch a check
// that has quietly stopped checking - an all-clear from a broken probe is worse than no probe.
const CANARY = 'gtceu:zzz_canary_this_must_not_exist'
const CANARY_TAG = 'minecraft:planks'

// Thirteen strings from the scripts are deliberately absent below. They look like ids but are not
// items: recipe ids passed as a recipe's name (gtceu:extruder/nan_certificate,
// kubejs:autoclave/nether_star, kubejs:inert_star, the allthemods:*_rotor_holder .id() calls, the
// kubejs:gtceu/greenhouse/ prefixes) and data keys (botanypots:crop, productivebees:bee_type,
// productivebees:neutronium), plus the gtceu:lathe_ / extrude_ / bend_ prefixes that allthemodium.js
// builds recipe ids from by concatenation ('gtceu:lathe_' + type + '_to_rod'), which a text scan
// cannot see through. They were reported on every run, which is how a check trains you to
// skim past it. The TAGS list drops '#gtceu:circuits/' for the same reason: miner.js builds that
// tag by concatenation ('#gtceu:circuits/' + tier).
//
// The gtceu:*_*_rotor_holder double-prefixed ids are NOT in that group - KubeJS
// prepends the tier to the name, so those are real items.
